Scope: cockpit.rs GUI transport and unit fixtures only, plus this command/evidence record. Wire types, logic, live.rs and UI remain untouched.

Mechanism:
- json_frame preserves NDJSON, version/capability and the <1MiB frame bound before enqueue. Oversize is a local error, not a writer-task failure.
- GuiIo owns independent reader and writer tasks. Incoming remains bounded8; outgoing is bounded64. Only the writer owns OwnedWriteHalf and awaits socket writes. Frames leave FIFO.
- Session::send retains its async signature for callers but contains no await: it uses try_send. A full queue returns public typed cockpit::Busy; the caller retains the exact original action/ID/bytes and drains events before retrying.
- Session::writer_ready returns an owned, Send capacity future that does not borrow Session, so the IO owner can select it alongside event(). It wakes without an inbound reply. No new Event variant or wire field.
- Writer-task error/death becomes Event::Disconnected even if the read side is alive. Dropping the connection aborts both tasks. receive() also observes connection/child death via event(), preserving the separately held private control pipes.
- Aster owns the C1i retry outbox for Input/Resize and generated Watch/Unwatch/Applied. Busy must be handled as pressure; Applied is enqueued only after prepare/publish. This change adds the transport primitive only.

